"https://api.github.com/users/i-hate-debugging/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-hate-debugging/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-hate-debugging/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-hate-debugging/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-hate-debugging/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-hate-debugging/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-hate-debugging/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-hate-debugging/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/i-hate-debugging/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-07T19:28:06Z","updated_at":"2026-09-07T19:28:24Z","body":"I tried fixing this, the pull request was:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123284\nI was able to reproduce this with extremely long lines in the script editor.\nThe issue was caused by syntax highlighting repeatedly processing the entire line during editor operations such as editing, undo, and redo.\nI opened a pull request that skips syntax highlighting for lines longer than 10,000 characters and caches the result. Normal lines are unaffected. The long line remains editable, and undo/redo preserve the text correctly.\nI also added a TextEdit regression test covering editing, undo, and redo on a 10,000-character line.\nManually tested on Windows with the patched Godot editor.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5574887280/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"spam"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5576362153","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/123246#issuecomment-5576362153"